"<div id=""mindx-private-practice-checklist"">

  <h2>Private Practice Preparation Checklist</h2>

  <div class=""subtitle"">
    A practical checklist for therapists preparing to launch
    and operate a private practice in the United States.
  </div>


  <!-- PROGRESS -->

  <div class=""progress-box"">

    <div class=""progress-top"">

      <span>Practice Preparation</span>

      <strong id=""ppProgressText"">
        0 / 52
      </strong>

    </div>

    <div class=""progress-track"">

      <div
        class=""progress-bar""
        id=""ppProgressBar"">
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>


  <!-- 1 BUSINESS FOUNDATION -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>1. Business Foundation</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Establish the basic business structure and identity of your practice.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Define your private practice model</strong>

        <small>
          Decide whether you plan to operate independently,
          as part of a group practice, or with additional clinicians.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Choose your business name</strong>

        <small>
          Select a professional name and verify applicable
          state and local naming requirements.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Choose a business structure</strong>

        <small>
          Evaluate whether a sole proprietorship, LLC, professional
          entity, corporation, or another structure is appropriate
          for your situation.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Register the business if required</strong>

        <small>
          Complete applicable state or local registration requirements
          for your chosen structure and location.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Check state and local requirements</strong>

        <small>
          Confirm applicable business licenses, professional entity
          requirements, permits, and local requirements.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Obtain an EIN</strong>

        <small>
          Apply for an Employer Identification Number through the IRS
          when applicable. The IRS provides EIN applications directly
          at no charge.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 2 FINANCIAL -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>2. Financial & Tax Setup</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Separate your business finances and establish a system for
      managing income, expenses, and taxes.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Open a business bank account</strong>

        <small>
          Establish a dedicated business checking account and keep
          business and personal funds appropriately separated.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set up business bookkeeping</strong>

        <small>
          Establish a system for tracking revenue, expenses,
          reimbursements, and other financial activity.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Choose an accounting or bookkeeping system</strong>

        <small>
          Select software or a bookkeeping process that works for
          your practice size and financial needs.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create a business budget</strong>

        <small>
          Estimate recurring expenses such as EHR, insurance,
          software, billing, marketing, office space, and professional fees.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Plan for estimated taxes</strong>

        <small>
          Determine how you will set aside funds and meet applicable
          federal, state, and local tax obligations.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Consult a qualified tax professional if needed</strong>

        <small>
          Consider professional guidance regarding entity structure,
          deductions, estimated taxes, retirement planning, or other
          business tax questions.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 3 LICENSURE -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>3. Licensure & Professional Requirements</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Confirm that your clinical practice structure is consistent
      with your professional license and applicable regulations.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Verify active professional license</strong>

        <small>
          Confirm that your license is active and that your planned
          services are within your scope of practice.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Review state private-practice requirements</strong>

        <small>
          Check your state licensing board and applicable state
          agencies for private-practice requirements.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Confirm telehealth requirements</strong>

        <small>
          Review requirements applicable to providing telehealth
          to clients in each state where you practice.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Maintain required professional credentials</strong>

        <small>
          Confirm continuing education, renewal, supervision,
          and other requirements applicable to your license.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 4 NPI -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>4. Provider Identification & Credentialing</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Prepare the provider identifiers and information commonly used
      for healthcare administration and insurance billing.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Obtain or verify your individual NPI</strong>

        <small>
          Make sure your Type 1 NPI information is current and
          accurately reflects your professional information.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Determine whether an organization NPI is applicable</strong>

        <small>
          If operating through an organization or entity, determine
          whether a Type 2 NPI is appropriate for your practice.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Update NPPES information</strong>

        <small>
          Review your provider information and keep applicable
          NPI records current.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Prepare credentialing information</strong>

        <small>
          Organize your license, NPI, education, malpractice insurance,
          CAQH information, practice address, and other commonly requested
          provider information.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Decide whether to accept insurance</strong>

        <small>
          Determine whether your practice will be private pay,
          insurance-based, or use a combination of payer models.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 5 INSURANCE -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>5. Insurance & Risk Management</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Put appropriate protections and risk-management processes in place.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Obtain professional liability insurance</strong>

        <small>
          Secure malpractice/professional liability coverage appropriate
          for your profession and practice model.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Review general business insurance needs</strong>

        <small>
          Consider whether additional business coverage is appropriate
          for your location, equipment, employees, or operations.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Review cyber/privacy risk</strong>

        <small>
          Consider appropriate safeguards and insurance coverage
          for electronic protected health information and technology risks.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 6 HIPAA -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>6. HIPAA, Privacy & Security</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Establish systems for protecting client information and
      maintaining appropriate privacy and security practices.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Choose HIPAA-appropriate technology</strong>

        <small>
          Review whether your EHR, telehealth platform, email,
          storage, and other systems are appropriate for handling
          protected health information.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Establish a privacy and security process</strong>

        <small>
          Create reasonable administrative, physical, and technical
          safeguards for client information.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Review Business Associate Agreements</strong>

        <small>
          Determine which vendors require appropriate business
          associate arrangements when applicable.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set up secure passwords and authentication</strong>

        <small>
          Use strong passwords, appropriate access controls,
          and multi-factor authentication where available.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 7 CLINICAL DOCUMENTATION -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>7. Clinical Documentation</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Prepare the documents and workflows you will use with clients.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Select an EHR</strong>

        <small>
          Choose an electronic health record system appropriate
          for your clinical, documentation, billing, and telehealth needs.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Prepare informed consent documentation</strong>

        <small>
          Establish appropriate informed consent and practice policies
          for your services.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Prepare Notice of Privacy Practices</strong>

        <small>
          Establish the applicable privacy documentation required
          for your practice.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Prepare telehealth consent and policies</strong>

        <small>
          If offering telehealth, establish appropriate telehealth
          procedures and documentation.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create clinical documentation templates</strong>

        <small>
          Prepare templates for intake assessments, progress notes,
          treatment planning, and discharge documentation as appropriate.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 8 FEES -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>8. Fees, Policies & Client Financials</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Make financial expectations clear before services begin.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set your standard session fee</strong>

        <small>
          Establish a fee that reflects your experience, market,
          overhead, desired income, and practice model.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create a cancellation and no-show policy</strong>

        <small>
          Clearly define your policy for late cancellations,
          missed appointments, and applicable fees.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Establish payment procedures</strong>

        <small>
          Decide how clients will pay, when payment is collected,
          and which payment methods you accept.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Prepare Good Faith Estimate procedures</strong>

        <small>
          If applicable, establish a process for providing required
          Good Faith Estimates to eligible self-pay or uninsured clients.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 9 BILLING -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>9. Billing & Revenue Cycle</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Build a reliable process for getting paid and tracking revenue.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Choose a billing workflow</strong>

        <small>
          Decide whether billing will be handled by you,
          your EHR, a billing service, or another arrangement.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set up payment processing</strong>

        <small>
          Establish a secure method for collecting client payments
          and understand applicable processing fees.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Establish an insurance claims workflow</strong>

        <small>
          If accepting insurance, determine how eligibility,
          claims, remittance, denials, and patient responsibility
          will be managed.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create a system for tracking accounts receivable</strong>

        <small>
          Monitor unpaid balances, outstanding claims,
          and other receivables.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 10 OPERATIONS -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>10. Practice Operations</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Build the day-to-day systems that keep your practice running smoothly.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set up a professional email</strong>

        <small>
          Create a professional email address and establish a secure
          communication workflow for client-related information.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Set up scheduling</strong>

        <small>
          Choose a scheduling system and establish your availability,
          appointment types, and cancellation settings.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create a client intake workflow</strong>

        <small>
          Map the process from initial inquiry through consultation,
          intake, consent, first session, and ongoing care.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Establish emergency and crisis procedures</strong>

        <small>
          Define how your practice will respond to urgent clinical
          situations, including appropriate local resources and procedures.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Establish records retention and disposal procedures</strong>

        <small>
          Create a process for maintaining, storing, and securely
          disposing of clinical records according to applicable requirements.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 11 MARKETING -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>11. Marketing & Client Acquisition</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Make it easy for appropriate prospective clients and referral
      sources to understand and find your practice.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create a professional website or profile</strong>

        <small>
          Clearly communicate your services, specialties,
          populations, location, availability, and contact process.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Create or update directory profiles</strong>

        <small>
          Review relevant therapist directories and professional
          profiles for accuracy and consistency.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Define your ideal client population</strong>

        <small>
          Identify the populations, concerns, and clinical areas
          you would most like your practice to serve.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Develop a referral strategy</strong>

        <small>
          Identify professional referral sources and create a
          sustainable approach to building referral relationships.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- 12 FINAL -->

  <div class=""category"">

    <h3>12. Ready to Open</h3>

    <p class=""category-description"">
      Complete a final review before accepting your first private-practice client.
    </p>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Test your complete intake process</strong>

        <small>
          Walk through the process yourself from inquiry and scheduling
          through payment, forms, telehealth, documentation, and follow-up.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Verify all public-facing information</strong>

        <small>
          Confirm that your website, directory profiles, fees,
          insurance information, contact information, and availability
          are accurate.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Confirm your financial systems are working</strong>

        <small>
          Test payment processing, business banking, bookkeeping,
          and billing workflows before opening.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>


    <label class=""check-item"">

      <input type=""checkbox"">

      <span>

        <strong>Complete a final compliance review</strong>

        <small>
          Review your practice setup against applicable state,
          professional, privacy, and business requirements.
        </small>

      </span>

    </label>

  </div>


  <!-- COMPLETION -->

  <div
    class=""completion-box""
    id=""ppCompletionBox"">

    <div class=""completion-title"">
      You're Ready to Review Your Launch Plan
    </div>

    <div class=""completion-text"">
      You've completed the checklist. Before opening your practice,
      review your setup with the appropriate professional or regulatory
      resources for your state and practice model.
    </div>

  </div>


  <!-- RESET -->

  <div class=""reset-area"">

    <button id=""ppResetChecklist"">
      Reset Checklist
    </button>

    <div class=""save-note"">
      Your progress is saved in this browser.
    </div>

  </div>


  <div class=""disclaimer"">

    This checklist is for educational and planning purposes only.
    Requirements vary by state, license type, business structure,
    payer, and practice model. It is not legal, tax, billing,
    or regulatory advice.

  </div>


</div>


